descriptions:
The project aims to support the Ministry of Health to streamline and harmonise the management of health regulations, ensuring adherence to Law No. 17 of 2023.

It will be conducted through several phases:
Phase 1: Proof of Concept Phase, which entails consolidation and categorisation of existing health regulations, identifying inconsistencies and gaps; 
Phase 2: Regulatory Database & Advance Search Phase, consisting creation of a comprehensive database with an advanced search function for efficient retrieval of relevant regulations;
Phase 3: Regulatory Framework System Phase, which will develop an actual system by perpetual licence to use; and 
Phase 4: Capacity Building Phase to disseminate knowledge for National health Policy Agency (BKPK) Ministry of Health personnel on system utilisation.
